# class A { m() { this.x } }  class B { m() { this.x } }  function run(o) { o.m() }  run(new A()); run(new B())
# In `o.m()` a function runs with a receiver as `this` only where the read of `m` from that receiver answers the function. The call has both methods as callees and both instances as receivers,
# and each method sees the instances of its own class alone.
